    "narrative": "For today\u2019s matchup, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is our clear anchor with a 76.07 efficiency score. His favorable park factors and the +2% bonus for targeting an opponent with a slow delivery\u2014which maximizes his stolen base potential\u2014make him the must-start of the day. We are also leaning heavily into our speed and platoon mismatches, with **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) and **Lawrence Butler** (68.16) representing our strongest secondary options. **Dylan Beavers** benefits immensely from a +16% park boost and the same stolen base efficiency bonus as **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, while **Lawrence Butler** is poised to exploit a high-efficiency matchup against Wesneski. **Bryce Harper** (67.36) remains a set-it-and-forget-it play, buoyed by a strong batting order position and solid xwOBA peripherals against Dobbins.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Zack Gelof**, who sits on the bench today with a 55.18 efficiency score. While his projection remains respectable, he was ultimately pushed out by the superior platoon utility of **JJ Bleday** (66.17) and the high-upside speed threat of **Justin Crawford**. We are carefully monitoring the performance of **Brendan Donovan** (47.78); while his leadoff spot provides value, his significant -15% dynamic platoon penalty against Boyd is a drag on his overall output. No major weather-related warnings are currently in effect, but we are keeping a close eye on the late-afternoon lineups, as any shuffling at the bottom of the order could necessitate a pivot for **Justin Crawford** or **Yainer Diaz** to preserve our limited game caps.",
